  overview='Mini farm animals make an appealing coordinated set for shelves, craft fairs and handmade presents. A shared body keeps the proportions consistent, while ears, snouts, woolly surface details and color turn one pattern into four recognizable characters.',
  stitches='**Shared body:** R1 6 sc in MR (6); R2 inc x6 (12); R3 (sc, inc) x6 (18); R4 (2 sc, inc) x6 (24); R5 (3 sc, inc) x6 (30); R6–R9 sc around (30); R10 (3 sc, dec) x6 (24); R11 (2 sc, dec) x6 (18); R12 (sc, dec) x6 (12); fill lightly, R13 dec x6 (6), close. **Cow:** Use cream body, embroider dark patches and sew two rounded ears plus two tiny horn motifs. **Sheep:** Work cream body, then add short loop stitches or small separately crocheted bobble-like tufts only if you are confident they are securely attached. **Pig:** Use pale pink body, embroider oval snout with darker pink and add triangular ears. **Chick:** Use yellow body with a tiny stitched orange beak and two small flat wings made from ch 4 and sc back.',
